{"id": "sevt_01MHNj8ECXQHVoLUFK82w3PL", "content": [{"text": "F-105 is a false positive and can't be exploited. I created one ticket draft marking it not exploitable with severity none.\n\n| ID | Rule | Location | Verdict | Severity | Reason |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| F-105 | SQL Injection | tests/fixtures/seed_db.py:10 | not_exploitable | none | The query is built by joining strings, but the only values joined in are the hardcoded `USERS` list (line 3). Nothing else in the repo calls this function. The app's only route is `/health` (app/main.py:6-8), and it doesn't use this file. |\n\n**Suggested fix (code quality, not security):** switch to a parameterized query, `conn.execute(\"INSERT INTO users VALUES (?, ?)\", (name, email))`, so this pattern doesn't get copied into production code. You could also tell the scanner to skip `tests/fixtures/` for this rule.\n\nI didn't open `config.py`. A search for \"seed\" across the repo found nothing outside the flagged file, so it isn't involved in this finding.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-26T20:54:16.165908Z", "type": "agent.message"}
